            <ArticleTitle>Erosion of the Nuss bar into the internal mammary artery 4 months after minimally invasive repair of pectus excavatum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2007.10.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The minimally invasive repair of pectus excavatum has become increasingly popular. Life-threatening complications have included bleeding and cardiac perforation. There have been a number of delayed cases of bleeding, many of which never demonstrated a clear source. We present a case of a delayed acute bleed from the Nuss bar eroding into the internal mammary artery 4 months after bar placement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
